e drinking (mean)\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"The age-adjusted † total annual number of binge drinks per adult who reported binge drinking increased significantly from 472 in 2011 to 529 in 2017.\"}]},{\"v\":\"percentage increase\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"were observed among those without a high school diploma (45.8%) and those with household incomes <$25,000 (23.9%)\"}]},{\"v\":\"binge drinking prevalence %\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"table 1\",\"q\":\"Binge drinking prevalence % †\"}]}],\"regression_fields\":null,\"public_health_question\":{\"v\":\"How did total annual binge drinks per adult who reported binge drinking change in the United States during 2011–2017, overall, by sociodemographic group and by state?\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"to assess trends in total annual binge drinks per adult who reported binge drinking in the United States overall and in the individual states\"}]},\"conditions\":[{\"v\":\"binge drinking\",\"role\":\"outcome\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"title\",\"q\":\"Trends in Total Binge Drinks per Adult Who Reported Binge Drinking — United States, 2011–2017\"}]}],\"study_design\":[{\"v\":\"cross-sectional\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"BRFSS is a state-based, random-digit–dialed landline and cellular telephone survey of noninstitutionalized, civilian U.S. adults aged ≥18 years\"}]},{\"v\":\"before/after or trend\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"Linear and quadratic trends of the total annual binge drinks per adult who reported binge drinking were assessed by orthogonal polynomial contrast\"}]}],\"data_source_type\":[{\"v\":\"national survey\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"CDC analyzed 2011–2017 BRFSS data\"}]}],\"data_source_named\":[{\"v\":\"Behavioral Risk Factor Surveillance System (BRFSS)\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"CDC analyzed 2011–2017 Behavioral Risk Factor Surveillance System (BRFSS) data\"}]}],\"setting\":{\"v\":\"mixed\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"in the United States overall and in the indivi